# Teferi's Reproach: "Choose target opponent. Until that player's next turn, they gain protection from everything and
# their life total can't change. All nonland permanents they control phase out." Bot1 (turn 3) floats {W}{R}{R} and
# cannot name itself as the target - "target opponent" (CR 115.1) - then casts it at Bot2: Bot2's Mox Ruby and Brazen
# Borrower phase out while their Tundra, a land, stays, and Bot1's own permanents do not phase out. Bot2 has protection
# from everything, so Bot1's Lightning Bolt can't target them (CR 702.16b, 702.16j). Bot1's Sunspine Lynx - "damage can't
# be prevented" - deals Bot2 1 damage for the Tundra: nothing is prevented, yet Bot2's life total can't change (CR
# 119.8). Bot2's next turn begins on turn 4, so both effects end (CR 611.2a) and the two permanents phase in during that
# untap step (CR 502.1). On turn 5 Bot1's Lightning Bolt reaches Bot2 for 3: Bot2's life is 17, which shows the Lynx's 1
# damage never changed it.

